WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:37.930
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:38.200 --> 01:44.030
[Small Town Remedy]

3
01:44.229 --> 01:46.720
[Episode 17]

4
01:46.970 --> 01:48.150
[Ambulance]

5
01:48.150 --> 01:49.240
[Fucheng Emergency Medical Rescue Center]

6
01:49.270 --> 01:52.880
[Ambulance]

7
01:59.560 --> 02:00.120
Come on.

8
02:02.200 --> 02:03.230
Careful. Careful.

9
02:03.230 --> 02:04.280
Move aside!

10
02:05.120 --> 02:06.310
Make way! Make way!

11
02:06.840 --> 02:07.710
Careful. This way.

12
02:07.710 --> 02:09.440
The patient's semiconscious.

13
02:09.840 --> 02:10.630
This way! This way!

14
02:10.630 --> 02:11.560
Let me take over.

15
02:12.120 --> 02:12.960
Careful. Careful.

16
02:12.960 --> 02:14.020
Careful. Careful.

17
02:24.910 --> 02:26.150
Sir, you want to talk?

18
02:26.400 --> 02:28.400
He wants to talk. Take it off for now.

19
02:32.310 --> 02:33.150
My son...

20
02:33.710 --> 02:35.150
Dad, I'm here. I'm here.

21
02:37.079 --> 02:38.840
I'm done for.

22
02:39.120 --> 02:39.870
Stop, Dad.

23
02:39.870 --> 02:40.680
Don't talk nonsense.

24
02:40.680 --> 02:41.960
Just relax.

25
02:42.360 --> 02:43.470
Look at this hospital,

26
02:43.470 --> 02:45.030
with all the high-tech equipment.

27
02:45.030 --> 02:46.840
And the doctors are all here.

28
02:46.870 --> 02:48.070
You won't be done for.

29
02:49.079 --> 02:50.520
Alright, that's enough.

30
02:50.680 --> 02:52.630
Sir, your blood oxygen level has dropped.

31
02:52.630 --> 02:54.079
It's okay. Don't worry.

32
02:54.079 --> 02:54.910
Your heart rate is a little high.

33
02:54.910 --> 02:55.870
Just relax,

34
02:55.870 --> 02:56.960
and your heart rate will go down.

35
02:56.960 --> 02:57.840
It's okay.

36
02:58.220 --> 02:59.930
[Priority for Patients with Acute Stroke]

37
02:58.710 --> 02:59.800
When the patient was brought in,

38
02:59.800 --> 03:01.360
his oxygen saturation was only 85%.

39
02:59.950 --> 03:01.470
[Priority for Seniors Aged 80 and Older]

40
03:01.400 --> 03:02.750
It could be a lung problem.

41
03:02.750 --> 03:03.800
85?

42
03:04.870 --> 03:06.560
That's a pretty good score.

43
03:06.800 --> 03:07.960
I told you you didn't have to be that concerned.

44
03:07.040 --> 03:12.110
[Wishing You a Speedy Recovery]

45
03:08.680 --> 03:09.870
An oxygen saturation below 90%

46
03:09.870 --> 03:10.800
means hypoxemia.

47
03:10.800 --> 03:11.470
At 85%,

48
03:11.470 --> 03:12.750
it's already very serious.

49
03:12.180 --> 03:18.310
[Priority for Patients with Acute Stroke]

50
03:14.630 --> 03:16.230
I thought 0 was dangerous.

51
03:16.230 --> 03:16.400
Then...

52
03:16.400 --> 03:17.630
Just stop blabbering.

53
03:17.630 --> 03:19.120
Does the patient have any medical history?

54
03:19.120 --> 03:20.590
Has he taken any medication recently?

55
03:20.590 --> 03:22.590
He had a pulmonary embolism before.

56
03:23.079 --> 03:24.960
He's been taking warfarin ever since,

57
03:24.960 --> 03:26.760
I think that's what it's called.

58
03:27.000 --> 03:28.860
Then, about 2 weeks ago,

59
03:28.880 --> 03:30.470
he developed a fever and cough.

60
03:30.470 --> 03:31.590
The doctor in town said

61
03:31.590 --> 03:32.960
it was bronchitis,

62
03:33.150 --> 03:33.840
so he got

63
03:33.840 --> 03:35.079
IV drips for half a month,

64
03:35.079 --> 03:36.680
but they didn't seem to help.

65
03:37.079 --> 03:39.030
Then he took licorice tablets

66
03:39.360 --> 03:41.430
and some cough and phlegm medicine,

67
03:41.430 --> 03:43.490
but those didn't seem to help either.

68
03:44.590 --> 03:46.590
This doesn't look like simple bronchitis.

69
03:46.590 --> 03:48.079
Then what could it be?

70
03:49.120 --> 03:50.650
It should be a lung disease.

71
03:50.910 --> 03:51.630
But

72
03:51.870 --> 03:53.960
if it were ordinary pneumonia,

73
03:54.190 --> 03:55.610
antibiotics should've helped

74
03:55.610 --> 03:56.960
after 2 weeks of treatment.

75
03:56.960 --> 03:57.710
The patient's having trouble breathing!

76
03:57.710 --> 03:59.079
His oxygen saturation is below 70%,

77
03:59.079 --> 04:00.150
and his blood pressure is also dropping!

78
04:00.150 --> 04:00.910
Prepare for intubation,

79
04:00.910 --> 04:02.110
and get him to the ICU!

80
04:02.560 --> 04:03.120
Come on!

81
04:03.630 --> 04:04.830
Move aside! Make way!

82
04:08.680 --> 04:09.340
Be careful.

83
04:09.710 --> 04:10.280
Careful.

84
04:18.209 --> 04:21.839
[Family Visitation Window]

85
04:21.600 --> 04:23.360
This is really strange.

86
04:24.600 --> 04:25.800
Look at the chest CT.

87
04:27.680 --> 04:30.000
There's consolidation and exudation in the right lower lobe,

88
04:30.000 --> 04:31.660
along with air bronchograms.

89
04:31.920 --> 04:33.780
Everything points to pneumonia.

90
04:34.630 --> 04:36.510
The township clinic started him on ceftriaxone

91
04:36.510 --> 04:37.510
and azithromycin,

92
04:37.510 --> 04:38.920
then switched to minocycline,

93
04:38.920 --> 04:40.070
but none of them worked.

94
04:39.909 --> 04:44.250
[Infective Waste]

95
04:40.600 --> 04:42.070
Either the bacteria are drug-resistant,

96
04:42.070 --> 04:44.070
or it's not ordinary pneumonia.

97
04:44.600 --> 04:46.600
That's what makes this so puzzling.

98
04:47.070 --> 04:48.090
If it's not pneumonia,

99
04:48.090 --> 04:49.290
what else could it be?

100
04:50.159 --> 04:51.680
But how are we supposed to treat it

101
04:51.680 --> 04:53.409
if we can't identify the cause?

102
04:59.480 --> 05:00.270
Try this.

103
05:01.040 --> 05:03.100
You stewed the green beans yourself?

104
05:06.870 --> 05:07.870
So good!

105
05:08.630 --> 05:11.560
I always eat at the cafeteria, and I'm getting sick of it.

106
05:11.560 --> 05:13.000
You really know how to cook green beans.

107
05:13.000 --> 05:13.560
Here,

108
05:14.830 --> 05:17.760
have some of this high-quality protein to go with it.

109
05:18.600 --> 05:19.390
Thanks.

110
05:21.680 --> 05:23.800
At least have something to eat or drink.

111
05:23.800 --> 05:25.400
The food's going to get cold.

112
05:27.510 --> 05:28.570
I have no appetite.

113
05:30.240 --> 05:32.170
Worried about Mr. Wu's condition?

114
05:32.680 --> 05:33.310
Yes.

115
05:33.430 --> 05:34.490
It's a tricky case.

116
05:34.750 --> 05:35.570
Even Li and Jin

117
05:35.600 --> 05:37.600
can't figure out what's causing it.

118
05:38.190 --> 05:39.480
Didn't he have a pulmonary embolism before?

119
05:39.480 --> 05:40.240
Could it be

120
05:40.240 --> 05:41.310
another one?

121
05:43.480 --> 05:45.630
He does have a history of pulmonary embolism,

122
05:45.630 --> 05:47.630
and he's been taking warfarin ever since.

123
05:47.630 --> 05:49.430
His D-dimer is normal this time,

124
05:49.480 --> 05:50.720
but he's had a persistent

125
05:50.720 --> 05:52.000
fever and cough.

126
05:52.720 --> 05:55.830
The X-rays look like an infection no matter how you look at them.

127
05:55.830 --> 05:56.750
How strange.

128
05:58.680 --> 06:00.360
Could it be tuberculosis?

129
06:01.000 --> 06:02.870
I suspected TB at first, too.

130
06:02.870 --> 06:03.510
But

131
06:03.510 --> 06:05.160
we did a TB smear

132
06:05.160 --> 06:06.430
and TB antibody test when he was admitted,

133
06:06.430 --> 06:07.510
and both came back negative.

134
06:07.510 --> 06:09.040
We have no evidence to support that diagnosis.

135
06:09.040 --> 06:11.070
If we can't figure out what's causing it,

136
06:11.070 --> 06:12.600
maybe we should persuade him

137
06:12.600 --> 06:13.270
to transfer to another hospital.

138
06:13.270 --> 06:15.400
We can't let this delay his treatment.

139
06:15.870 --> 06:17.670
I suggested that from the start,

140
06:18.120 --> 06:20.000
but they don't want the hassle.

141
06:20.310 --> 06:21.390
Their family's not well-off.

142
06:21.390 --> 06:25.320
Coming to our Xiaoximen Hospital is already stretching their budget.

143
06:25.870 --> 06:27.530
If only Zhengliang were here.

144
06:28.680 --> 06:30.740
How would it be better if he were here?

145
06:30.920 --> 06:32.050
Am I not good enough?

146
06:32.360 --> 06:33.960
Can't you discuss it with me?

147
06:34.390 --> 06:35.720
Even if I discuss it with you, can you solve it?

148
06:35.720 --> 06:37.070
Why can't I?

149
06:39.680 --> 06:41.270
Of course I can.

150
06:42.430 --> 06:43.720
Didn't you just say

151
06:43.720 --> 06:44.830
you suspected TB?

152
06:44.870 --> 06:46.870
You have to trust your own judgment.

153
06:47.430 --> 06:49.310
What's the point of me trusting myself?

154
06:49.310 --> 06:50.790
This is a matter of life and death.

155
06:50.790 --> 06:52.190
I can't just go with my gut.

156
06:52.190 --> 06:53.790
I need scientific evidence.

157
06:54.190 --> 06:55.190
It's okay.

158
06:55.240 --> 06:57.920
T-There will always be a way.

159
06:58.510 --> 06:59.390
Don't worry.

160
07:01.390 --> 07:02.480
Alright, you go eat.

161
07:02.480 --> 07:03.810
I'll take another look.

162
07:17.240 --> 07:18.360
But from the smear

163
07:18.360 --> 07:19.360
and the antibody test...

164
07:18.920 --> 07:21.830
[Quiet]

165
07:19.360 --> 07:20.960
Let's put those aside for now

166
07:21.000 --> 07:22.560
and think about what President always says:

167
07:22.560 --> 07:24.310
look at the patient as a whole.

168
07:24.310 --> 07:25.560
The patient's elderly,

169
07:25.560 --> 07:27.040
his family isn't well-off,

170
07:27.040 --> 07:28.240
he drinks heavily,

171
07:28.950 --> 07:30.390
and he's visibly emaciated

172
07:30.390 --> 07:31.560
and malnourished.

173
07:31.950 --> 07:33.080
He's had a prolonged

174
07:33.110 --> 07:34.000
fever and cough,

175
07:34.000 --> 07:35.750
and antibiotics haven't worked.

176
07:35.750 --> 07:36.750
All these factors

177
07:36.750 --> 07:38.159
point to TB.

178
07:38.360 --> 07:39.190
Plus,

179
07:39.240 --> 07:40.870
the positive rate for tubercle bacillus smears

180
07:40.870 --> 07:41.390
is relatively low.

181
07:41.390 --> 07:43.260
Just because the first test was negative

182
07:43.260 --> 07:45.000
doesn't necessarily rule out TB.

183
07:45.000 --> 07:47.000
Aren't you being a bit argumentative?

184
07:47.000 --> 07:47.390
Wait,

185
07:47.390 --> 07:49.120
how is that being argumentative?

186
07:49.120 --> 07:50.500
You just don't trust my judgment,

187
07:50.500 --> 07:51.040
do you?

188
07:51.040 --> 07:54.510
-If Liu Zhengliang were here… -It wouldn't matter who was here!

189
07:54.510 --> 07:56.310
The scans are right there.

190
07:56.480 --> 07:58.409
This patient simply can't have TB.

191
07:59.310 --> 08:00.810
Medically speaking, there's no such thing

192
08:00.810 --> 08:02.670
as a 100% definitive conclusion.

193
08:02.680 --> 08:04.880
You can't just rule out the possibility

194
08:05.160 --> 08:06.160
Dr. Che mentioned.

195
08:06.160 --> 08:07.310
Chen Junnan.

196
08:09.310 --> 08:10.750
Can you stop making things more complicated?

197
08:10.750 --> 08:12.600
How am I making things more complicated?

198
08:12.600 --> 08:14.360
We have no other leads, do we?

199
08:15.000 --> 08:16.920
Then why not try

200
08:17.070 --> 08:17.950
Dr. Che's approach?

201
08:17.950 --> 08:19.550
How are we supposed to try it?

202
08:19.680 --> 08:22.630
Doctors have to take responsibility for what they say.

203
08:22.630 --> 08:24.430
This isn't like shopping for clothes,

204
08:24.430 --> 08:25.510
where you can just try something on at random, okay?

205
08:25.510 --> 08:27.160
How is that irresponsible?

206
08:27.190 --> 08:29.120
And how is it just trying something at random?

207
08:29.120 --> 08:30.120
Dr. Che has a reasoned hypothesis,

208
08:30.120 --> 08:31.630
doesn't she?

209
08:31.630 --> 08:32.150
Junnan...

210
08:32.150 --> 08:33.360
Don't interrupt.

211
08:33.630 --> 08:34.440
Jin.

212
08:33.850 --> 08:40.600
[ICU]

213
08:36.870 --> 08:37.909
Did we collect a sputum sample from the patient

214
08:37.909 --> 08:39.770
before he was admitted to the ICU?

215
08:39.960 --> 08:40.789
Yes, once.

216
08:40.789 --> 08:41.850
Once isn't enough.

217
08:43.750 --> 08:44.750
We need 3 samples

218
08:44.960 --> 08:46.440
to ensure an adequate concentration,

219
08:46.440 --> 08:48.080
so we can test them for

220
08:48.080 --> 08:49.200
TB DNA.

221
08:49.320 --> 08:50.150
But

222
08:50.150 --> 08:52.010
our hospital can't run that test.

223
08:52.910 --> 08:54.440
I'll contact No. 1 Hospital

224
08:55.150 --> 08:56.600
and take the samples there myself.

225
08:56.600 --> 08:58.360
But our whole department is swamped.

226
08:58.360 --> 08:58.840
Who's going to take them?

227
08:58.840 --> 09:00.600
I will. I'll drive them over.

228
09:00.670 --> 09:01.630
And one test won't be enough—

229
09:01.630 --> 09:02.550
we need 3.

230
09:02.570 --> 09:04.120
We can't draw any conclusions

231
09:04.120 --> 09:05.120
until we get all 3 results.

232
09:05.120 --> 09:05.720
Come on...

233
09:05.720 --> 09:07.520
Don't you think that's a hassle?

234
09:08.110 --> 09:09.770
I've got nothing better to do.

235
09:10.270 --> 09:12.440
I'm the perfect person for the job.

236
09:20.890 --> 09:23.650
[Dream Garden Themed Hotel]

237
09:23.600 --> 09:26.260
There are so many small appliance repair shops.

238
09:29.000 --> 09:30.480
So this is the so-called

239
09:30.510 --> 09:31.670
"love hotel"?

240
09:33.000 --> 09:33.910
You bet.

241
09:35.000 --> 09:35.790
This place

242
09:36.030 --> 09:37.240
used to be an ordinary

243
09:37.510 --> 09:39.260
little in.

244
09:39.440 --> 09:41.040
It was renovated 3 years ago.

245
09:41.390 --> 09:42.270
Some idiot designer

246
09:42.270 --> 09:43.840
came out of nowhere

247
09:43.960 --> 09:46.200
and claimed this kind of decor would bring in more business.

248
09:46.200 --> 09:47.530
That woman believed him

249
09:47.960 --> 09:49.240
and poured a ton of money into it.

250
09:49.240 --> 09:50.720
But after the renovation,

251
09:50.750 --> 09:52.030
business was even worse than before.

252
09:52.030 --> 09:53.030
That woman?

253
09:54.120 --> 09:55.050
He means his mom.

254
09:58.510 --> 10:00.840
That the... the what?

255
10:04.440 --> 10:06.170
What does it have to do with you?

256
10:06.600 --> 10:07.840
Dream theme.

257
10:08.240 --> 10:09.370
Oh, so it's "theme".

258
10:12.240 --> 10:13.390
But wouldn't it be a bit weird for me

259
10:13.390 --> 10:14.790
to be staying here alone?

260
10:15.000 --> 10:15.750
Yeah.

261
10:15.750 --> 10:17.440
It's pretty weird and inappropriate.

262
10:17.440 --> 10:18.750
Why don't you find somewhere else?

263
10:18.750 --> 10:19.670
No way.

264
10:20.390 --> 10:21.840
Aren't you staying here alone too?

265
10:21.840 --> 10:22.240
What,

266
10:22.240 --> 10:23.840
you can stay here but I can't?

267
10:24.080 --> 10:25.510
I'm staying here because it's cheap.

268
10:25.510 --> 10:26.440
30 yuan a day.

269
10:26.440 --> 10:27.080
You won't find a deal like that anywhere else.

270
10:27.080 --> 10:27.940
I'm broke, too.

271
10:27.960 --> 10:28.870
I want a cheap place, too.

272
10:28.870 --> 10:29.600
Sis.

273
10:31.510 --> 10:32.970
For you, it's 20 yuan a day,

274
10:33.120 --> 10:34.510
and you get a free bottle of soy milk.

275
10:34.510 --> 10:35.630
You are so nice.

276
10:35.630 --> 10:37.760
No need. Just charge me the same as him.

277
10:38.550 --> 10:39.390
Give me that

278
10:39.390 --> 10:41.630
t-theme thing.

279
10:41.630 --> 10:42.790
D-D-Dream.

280
10:43.200 --> 10:44.400
Let me experience it.

281
10:53.150 --> 10:54.080
Look at Pink.

282
10:54.080 --> 10:56.910
The second he heard he had to carry the suitcase, he took off.

283
10:56.910 --> 10:58.030
So you do realize

284
10:58.030 --> 10:59.550
this suitcase is freaking heavy, huh?

285
10:59.550 --> 11:01.510
How do you think I hauled it all the way here?

286
11:01.510 --> 11:02.440
It's your own suitcase.

287
11:02.440 --> 11:03.870
Why should someone else carry it for you?

288
11:03.870 --> 11:05.550
I never asked him to carry it for me.

289
11:04.530 --> 11:06.090
[Friendly Reminder: Surveillance Cameras in Use— Please Be Mindful of Your Words and Actions]

290
11:07.390 --> 11:08.200
Hold on.

291
11:10.030 --> 11:11.430
Let's get this straight.

292
11:12.240 --> 11:13.440
When are you leaving?

293
11:21.550 --> 11:22.550
What do you want?

294
11:26.750 --> 11:28.510
That depends on when you leave.

295
11:28.510 --> 11:29.770
I leave when you leave.

296
11:30.670 --> 11:31.870
Stop messing around.

297
11:32.390 --> 11:33.270
What if I stay here

298
11:33.270 --> 11:34.530
for the rest of my life?

299
11:35.390 --> 11:36.720
Like you really mean it.

300
11:36.960 --> 11:39.630
It snows here in winter too.

301
11:43.550 --> 11:45.670
Didn't you have something to say to me?

302
11:45.670 --> 11:46.480
Say it now.

303
11:59.390 --> 12:00.320
So...

304
12:01.600 --> 12:02.670
After I finish,

305
12:03.270 --> 12:05.070
you'll just send me away, right?

306
12:08.630 --> 12:10.080
How dare you nod?

307
12:11.510 --> 12:12.550
I'll tell you

308
12:12.670 --> 12:13.720
when I leave.

309
12:16.630 --> 12:18.030
Are you coming in with me?

310
12:28.550 --> 12:29.680
Wait, what's wrong?

311
12:34.870 --> 12:35.870
See if you sink in.

312
12:38.270 --> 12:39.550
I'm already sinking!

313
12:39.720 --> 12:41.240
Why is it so wobbly?

314
12:41.600 --> 12:43.440
It feels like...

315
12:43.750 --> 12:45.750
Like I've had my spine pulled out.

316
12:46.270 --> 12:47.600
Is that why you yelled?

317
12:48.510 --> 12:50.510
H-Have you ever slept on a waterbed?

318
12:50.750 --> 12:51.480
No.

319
12:51.480 --> 12:52.650
There you go, then.

320
12:54.320 --> 12:56.120
T-This is so wild.

321
12:56.120 --> 12:57.250
Sleeping in this...

322
12:58.320 --> 12:59.150
What's the theme of this room again?

323
12:59.150 --> 13:00.440
The Caribbean?

324
13:01.080 --> 13:02.680
Why do you insist on staying?

325
13:11.200 --> 13:12.000
You...

326
13:12.360 --> 13:14.690
Why are you in such a hurry to make me leave?

327
13:19.120 --> 13:19.870
I'm scared.

328
13:23.120 --> 13:23.870
Scared of me?

329
13:24.910 --> 13:25.720
Yes.

330
13:26.390 --> 13:27.200
Of you.

331
13:28.910 --> 13:29.970
And of myself, too.

332
13:52.480 --> 13:53.200
When I came here,

333
13:53.200 --> 13:54.730
I'd already made up my mind.

334
13:59.720 --> 14:01.480
I'm not here for a fling.

335
14:05.870 --> 14:07.070
I want to take you home

336
14:10.910 --> 14:12.200
and build a relationship with you,

337
14:12.200 --> 14:13.200
one with a future,

338
14:14.200 --> 14:15.270
a journey,

339
14:19.270 --> 14:21.120
and a happy ending.

340
14:21.510 --> 14:22.600
I can't go back.

341
14:22.840 --> 14:24.510
B-But why?

342
14:25.030 --> 14:26.960
What do you mean, you can't go back?

343
14:28.150 --> 14:29.790
There are plenty of illnesses in the world that can't be cured,

344
14:29.790 --> 14:31.000
but yours isn't one of them.

345
14:31.000 --> 14:32.630
It is. I'm a doctor.

346
14:32.630 --> 14:34.360
Like doctors know everything.

347
14:35.150 --> 14:36.610
So what if you're a doctor?

348
14:36.750 --> 14:38.750
"One cannot save oneself, nor can a doctor heal himself."

349
14:38.750 --> 14:39.550
You know that?

350
14:39.840 --> 14:41.200
Even audiobooks say so.

351
14:42.840 --> 14:43.630
What?

352
14:49.000 --> 14:50.200
You two are busy, huh?

353
14:53.550 --> 14:55.320
Well, I saw the door was open,

354
14:55.320 --> 14:57.480
so I wanted to ask if you need anything.

355
14:58.750 --> 14:59.840
I-I'll come back later.

356
14:59.840 --> 15:01.040
Cut it out. Come back.

357
15:02.240 --> 15:03.300
What's wrong, Sis?

358
15:04.030 --> 15:05.870
We're both dressed properly.

359
15:06.030 --> 15:07.320
What can't you talk to us?

360
15:07.320 --> 15:08.110
What is it?

361
15:09.720 --> 15:10.480
Well,

362
15:11.360 --> 15:12.150
sis,

363
15:13.320 --> 15:14.150
do you have any plans

364
15:14.150 --> 15:15.360
for the next few days?

365
15:18.910 --> 15:20.000
Not for now.

366
15:21.150 --> 15:22.150
Here's the thing.

367
15:23.240 --> 15:24.320
You see,

368
15:24.480 --> 15:26.080
Zhengliang promised

369
15:26.360 --> 15:27.750
to hang out with me for a few days.

370
15:27.750 --> 15:29.280
When did I promise you that?

371
15:30.320 --> 15:31.120
Move.

372
15:33.240 --> 15:34.030
But...

373
15:36.790 --> 15:38.000
We agreed on that

374
15:38.000 --> 15:39.530
when we discussed the rent,

375
15:41.120 --> 15:41.790
didn't we?

376
15:41.790 --> 15:43.020
That I... I...

377
15:43.120 --> 15:44.240
I'd give you a discount,

378
15:44.240 --> 15:45.700
and you'd hang out with me.

379
15:45.750 --> 15:46.910
I even helped you submit

380
15:46.910 --> 15:47.870
your resume.

381
15:48.030 --> 15:49.720
Pink! Pink!

382
15:53.030 --> 15:53.720
Look at him.

383
15:53.720 --> 15:54.360
What did he

384
15:55.360 --> 15:56.720
promise to do with you?

385
15:57.200 --> 15:58.200
Count me in.

386
15:59.320 --> 16:01.550
That's exactly what I meant.

387
16:01.750 --> 16:02.550
Right?

388
16:03.150 --> 16:03.960
Well,

389
16:04.150 --> 16:06.150
Sis, you just got here.

390
16:06.510 --> 16:07.320
Is there anywhere

391
16:07.320 --> 16:08.510
you'd like to go?

392
16:09.000 --> 16:10.120
I don't know anyone or anything around here.

393
16:10.120 --> 16:11.520
How am I supposed to know?

394
16:15.670 --> 16:16.480
Perfect.

395
16:17.270 --> 16:18.480
I know

396
16:18.670 --> 16:19.870
just the place.

397
16:20.910 --> 16:22.570
I promise you'll have a blast.

398
16:23.550 --> 16:24.680
It'll be really fun.

399
16:33.030 --> 16:33.960
You wait there for the results.

400
16:33.960 --> 16:34.910
I'll head back to the ICU and wait for the samples.

401
16:34.910 --> 16:37.570
Don't worry. I'll get them to you as soon as I can.

402
16:40.670 --> 16:41.470
[For Laboratory Testing Only]

403
16:51.750 --> 16:52.670
Don't worry.

404
16:52.840 --> 16:54.270
It's normal not to get it on the first try.

405
16:54.270 --> 16:56.000
You don't need to tell me. Go on.

406
17:19.109 --> 17:19.920
How is it?

407
17:20.720 --> 17:21.680
Guess what?

408
17:21.920 --> 17:22.750
Let me see.

409
17:23.680 --> 17:24.670
Guess first.

410
17:29.000 --> 17:29.880
They found it.

411
17:30.950 --> 17:32.000
It's TB.

412
17:33.070 --> 17:34.730
The cause has been confirmed!

413
17:35.920 --> 17:36.640
You won.

414
17:37.400 --> 17:38.630
We won.

415
17:41.920 --> 17:42.720
Thank you.

416
17:52.640 --> 17:52.920
Dr. Jin.

417
17:52.920 --> 17:53.550
The new patient's

418
17:53.550 --> 17:54.680
test results are in.

419
17:54.830 --> 17:55.760
It's confirmed.

420
17:56.350 --> 17:57.400
It's TB.

421
17:57.960 --> 17:58.750
We can now transfer the patient

422
17:58.750 --> 18:00.310
to a negative-pressure isolation room,

423
18:00.310 --> 18:01.790
call the infectious disease hospital for a consultation,

424
18:01.790 --> 18:04.520
and start anti-TB treatment as soon as possible.

425
18:05.100 --> 18:06.020
That's great!

426
18:06.830 --> 18:08.270
He really came through.

427
18:08.400 --> 18:09.240
Can you tell what Li

428
18:09.240 --> 18:10.750
and Jin have written

429
18:10.750 --> 18:11.960
in their eyes?

430
18:12.480 --> 18:13.240
What?

431
18:13.480 --> 18:14.480
"Respect!"

432
18:15.000 --> 18:16.310
In big, bold letters!

433
18:17.110 --> 18:18.960
We make a great team, don't we?

434
18:19.720 --> 18:22.110
If it weren't for your sharp diagnosis

435
18:23.030 --> 18:24.720
and my quick reflexes,

436
18:23.730 --> 18:27.080
[To the Ob-GYN ward] [To the Operating Room]

437
18:25.200 --> 18:26.860
we'd have delayed treatment.

438
18:27.200 --> 18:29.550
Just think how much the patient would've suffered.

439
18:29.550 --> 18:31.400
Come on, admit it.

440
18:32.110 --> 18:33.510
I'm pretty much

441
18:34.030 --> 18:35.160
on Liu Zhengliang's level now,

442
18:35.160 --> 18:36.720
aren't I?

443
18:39.000 --> 18:40.720
Not quite.

444
18:41.240 --> 18:43.570
You two aren't even in the same dimension.

445
18:43.640 --> 18:45.200
What do you mean, not in the same dimension?

446
18:45.200 --> 18:45.960
What,

447
18:47.240 --> 18:50.350
is he in the first dimension and I'm in the second or something?

448
18:50.350 --> 18:52.150
Come on, give me a little praise.

449
18:52.880 --> 18:54.000
Just a little.

450
19:22.720 --> 19:23.510
Lyu.

451
19:24.000 --> 19:24.960
What's going on?

452
19:26.440 --> 19:27.240
It's nothing.

453
19:28.000 --> 19:31.400
The NHC is conducting a joint audit with the tax authorities.

454
20:31.920 --> 20:33.680
Come on, bread, bread.

455
20:34.750 --> 20:36.750
Bread, bread. Come on, bread.

456
20:37.960 --> 20:38.960
Help yourselves.

457
20:42.070 --> 20:43.240
Come on.

458
20:43.880 --> 20:44.880
Help yourselves.

459
20:45.790 --> 20:46.450
Here you go.

460
20:46.880 --> 20:47.830
Help yourselves.

461
20:47.830 --> 20:48.750
Come on.

462
20:49.510 --> 20:50.480
There's enough for everyone.

463
20:50.480 --> 20:51.830
Ask me if it's not enough.

464
20:51.830 --> 20:52.480
Come on.

465
20:52.830 --> 20:53.750
No, thanks.

466
20:53.750 --> 20:54.550
My hands are too dirty.

467
20:54.550 --> 20:55.880
Are there any wet wipes?

468
20:55.880 --> 20:57.240
Good job, everyone.

469
20:57.270 --> 20:57.880
You're not eating?

470
20:57.880 --> 20:58.340
I'm not.

471
20:58.350 --> 20:59.440
I'm so tired.

472
20:59.790 --> 21:01.320
Being an extra is so tiring.

473
21:01.510 --> 21:04.270
I think being an extra is fun.

474
21:05.310 --> 21:06.200
What's fun about it?

475
21:06.200 --> 21:07.400
Look at this steep slope.

476
21:07.400 --> 21:09.130
How many times have we run up it?

477
21:09.750 --> 21:10.550
We made

478
21:12.160 --> 21:13.490
12 round trips, I think.

479
21:15.200 --> 21:15.960
Shooting scenes like this

480
21:15.960 --> 21:17.290
must use up a lot of film.

481
21:19.160 --> 21:19.750
No, Sis.

482
21:21.200 --> 21:22.960
It's all digital cameras now.

483
21:23.110 --> 21:24.480
They don't use film anymore.

484
21:24.480 --> 21:25.610
You know quite a lot.

485
21:28.270 --> 21:29.670
I've done some research.

486
21:30.110 --> 21:31.030
I have...

487
21:33.550 --> 21:35.750
I've always wanted to experience

488
21:35.830 --> 21:37.430
what it's like to be an extra,

489
21:38.790 --> 21:40.520
and today I finally got to do it.

490
21:41.400 --> 21:42.200
What a blast!

491
21:44.440 --> 21:45.680
You had your blast.

492
21:45.680 --> 21:46.960
But my legs are about to cramp.

493
21:46.960 --> 21:48.690
I'm almost half dead, you know?

494
21:51.000 --> 21:51.590
I mean,

495
21:52.240 --> 21:53.790
this is all the production crew gave us to drink?

496
21:53.790 --> 21:55.000
It's freezing cold.

497
21:56.200 --> 21:57.800
Does this crew not have that?

498
21:58.440 --> 21:59.960
Don't stars usually treat people

499
21:59.960 --> 22:01.790
to bubble tea or something?

500
22:01.830 --> 22:03.230
Don't the extras get any?

501
22:03.960 --> 22:05.310
You should be grateful we got this, Sis.

502
22:05.310 --> 22:06.000
Is that so?

503
22:07.070 --> 22:08.000
Hey, beautiful!

504
22:09.440 --> 22:09.960
Me?

505
22:09.960 --> 22:10.510
A-Are you talking to me?

506
22:10.510 --> 22:11.480
Yes, you.

507
22:11.880 --> 22:12.240
We've got a role

508
22:12.240 --> 22:13.480
for a battlefield nurse here.

509
22:13.480 --> 22:14.340
Can you play it?

510
22:16.750 --> 22:17.640
Look at that.

511
22:17.920 --> 22:19.070
I'm a natural beauty.

512
22:19.070 --> 22:20.200
Even with makeup like this,

513
22:20.200 --> 22:21.640
I can't hide my good looks.

514
22:21.640 --> 22:23.200
You're the only woman here.

515
22:24.000 --> 22:25.400
You deserve the cramps.

516
22:26.920 --> 22:27.920
No, thanks, man.

517
22:27.920 --> 22:29.920
Let me cool off a bit. I'm exhausted.

518
22:30.070 --> 22:31.330
I'm sweating baskets.

519
22:31.510 --> 22:32.830
It's "sweating buckets."

520
22:32.830 --> 22:34.720
Beautiful, this role has lines.

521
22:34.720 --> 22:35.780
I'll pay you extra.

522
22:37.110 --> 22:37.790
Sis.

523
22:40.110 --> 22:41.000
It's a great opportunity.

524
22:41.000 --> 22:41.640
What do you mean?

525
22:41.640 --> 22:42.840
You've got to take it.

526
22:43.550 --> 22:44.920
Will it cover 3 bubble teas?

527
22:44.920 --> 22:46.500
It'll cover at least 6.

528
22:48.270 --> 22:49.070
Wait for me.

529
22:49.550 --> 22:51.110
-Come on! I'll do it! -Alright! Come on.

530
22:51.110 --> 22:52.030
Be careful.

531
22:53.440 --> 22:54.070
Buddy.

532
22:54.200 --> 22:55.680
Can you give me a little hint about the scene?

533
22:55.680 --> 22:57.960
I'm pretty good at crying scenes and stuff.

534
22:57.960 --> 22:59.480
Your character is all about excitement,

535
22:59.480 --> 22:59.880
-passion, and... -Excitement?

536
22:59.880 --> 23:00.960
Right, and killing enemies.

537
23:00.960 --> 23:03.160
So I just scream my head off like before?

538
23:03.440 --> 23:04.240
Director.

539
23:04.750 --> 23:06.350
What do you think of her?

540
23:07.790 --> 23:10.240
This makeup might make it hard to see what I really look like.

541
23:10.240 --> 23:11.570
She's decent-looking.

542
23:11.790 --> 23:12.550
Alright, let's go with her.

543
23:12.550 --> 23:13.350
Hurry up and get changed.

544
23:13.350 --> 23:14.480
Okay, got it.

545
23:15.110 --> 23:17.030
What do you mean "decent-looking"?

546
23:17.030 --> 23:18.270
Alright, wardrobe and makeup.

547
23:18.270 --> 23:18.720
Come over here.

548
23:18.720 --> 23:19.790
Clean her face up

549
23:19.790 --> 23:21.240
and get her changed.

550
23:21.240 --> 23:22.000
Here.

551
23:22.350 --> 23:23.920
These are Nurse Qian's lines.

552
23:23.920 --> 23:25.050
Read them carefully

553
23:25.200 --> 23:25.750
and memorize them.

554
23:25.750 --> 23:27.880
I'll run through them with you in a bit.

555
23:28.680 --> 23:30.480
Soldiers over there, come here.

556
23:37.550 --> 23:41.160
[Monitor]

557
23:53.190 --> 23:58.460
[Monitor]

558
23:56.480 --> 23:58.010
How's it going, beautiful?

559
23:58.640 --> 23:59.920
Here, I'll run through them with you.

560
23:59.920 --> 24:02.030
Buddy, you...

561
24:02.030 --> 24:02.830
Could you

562
24:02.960 --> 24:03.830
run through it for me first?

563
24:03.830 --> 24:04.960
Or is there

564
24:04.960 --> 24:06.000
an audio version of the script?

565
24:06.000 --> 24:07.110
Maybe you can talk to the director.

566
24:07.110 --> 24:08.310
Audio version?

567
24:08.510 --> 24:09.920
Wait, you can't read?

568
24:10.270 --> 24:12.390
[Monitor]

569
24:10.880 --> 24:11.880
Um, well...

570
24:11.880 --> 24:12.550
Um,

571
24:12.920 --> 24:13.720
I'm sorry.

572
24:13.830 --> 24:14.750
We're in a hurry,

573
24:14.750 --> 24:15.590
so she's out.

574
24:15.640 --> 24:17.550
Go on, change into your own clothes.

575
24:17.550 --> 24:19.030
But we had a deal!

576
24:17.800 --> 24:20.890
[Monitor]

577
24:19.030 --> 24:19.690
You guys...

578
24:36.270 --> 24:37.750
You were so cool today.

579
24:37.920 --> 24:39.550
Seriously. Such a real man.

580
24:39.830 --> 24:41.030
So tough and badass.

581
24:41.480 --> 24:43.880
I just didn't want you to embarrass yourself.

582
24:43.880 --> 24:46.240
If you're not cut out for the job, don't force it.

583
24:46.240 --> 24:47.160
Who said I wanted this gig?

584
24:47.160 --> 24:49.220
He's the one who wanted it, remember?

585
24:51.200 --> 24:52.350
Anyway,

586
24:52.590 --> 24:54.050
I appreciate what you did.

587
24:57.400 --> 24:58.860
It's just that sometimes,

588
24:59.240 --> 25:01.350
I forget that I'm sick.

589
25:02.240 --> 25:03.640
I'm sure you understand.

590
25:05.590 --> 25:06.440
But then

591
25:08.400 --> 25:10.860
life has a way of reminding you out of nowhere

592
25:11.480 --> 25:13.680
that you two aren't like everyone else.

593
25:13.720 --> 25:14.790
You two are sick.

594
25:20.790 --> 25:21.720
You two are sick?

595
25:23.510 --> 25:24.640
Yeah. Minor issues.

596
25:25.440 --> 25:26.920
If you're sick, you need to get treated.

597
25:26.920 --> 25:27.720
Right?

598
25:28.310 --> 25:29.110
See?

599
25:29.510 --> 25:30.550
Even your buddy here knows

600
25:30.550 --> 25:32.150
sick people need treatment.

601
25:32.510 --> 25:33.680
Mine's terminal.

602
25:33.880 --> 25:34.830
There's no cure.

603
25:36.880 --> 25:38.550
You also have a terminal illness, bro?

604
25:38.550 --> 25:39.590
What's it to you?

605
25:39.590 --> 25:41.190
And what do you mean, "also"?

606
25:42.550 --> 25:44.200
I was just asking.

607
25:44.590 --> 25:45.790
Poor choice of words.

608
25:58.480 --> 25:59.310
Give me one.

609
26:02.750 --> 26:03.680
Unfortunately,

610
26:03.720 --> 26:05.050
it's the last one again.

611
26:05.240 --> 26:06.550
What are the odds?

612
26:07.070 --> 26:08.470
Let me see your candy tin.

613
26:10.750 --> 26:11.000
Well, bro,

614
26:11.000 --> 26:12.440
what's there to see?

615
26:12.440 --> 26:13.440
What's the harm?

616
26:13.440 --> 26:14.510
Your buddy wants to see it, so let him.

617
26:14.510 --> 26:15.480
Come on. What's the big deal?

618
26:15.480 --> 26:16.480
Quit stalling.

619
26:17.240 --> 26:18.720
Hey, why are you so stingy?

620
26:18.720 --> 26:20.180
There are still some left,

621
26:20.240 --> 26:21.970
yet you told me there were none.

622
26:25.240 --> 26:27.200
This isn't candy. It's medicine.

623
26:29.070 --> 26:29.830
Medicine?

624
26:30.960 --> 26:32.000
Are you sick?

625
26:33.310 --> 26:34.590
What kind of medicine is this?

626
26:34.590 --> 26:36.320
Why put medicine in a candy tin?

627
26:38.640 --> 26:39.840
Just a minor illness.

628
26:40.510 --> 26:41.640
I just thought

629
26:42.270 --> 26:43.550
pill bottles were ugly,

630
26:43.550 --> 26:44.510
and this tin

631
26:44.510 --> 26:45.640
suits me better.

632
26:46.350 --> 26:47.240
Besides,

633
26:47.590 --> 26:49.400
it's not some controlled substance.

634
26:49.400 --> 26:50.460
Just painkillers.

635
26:53.310 --> 26:54.000
Zhou Zheng.

636
26:54.200 --> 26:55.000
Tell me the truth.

637
26:55.000 --> 26:56.310
What's your condition?

638
26:56.310 --> 26:58.240
Come on, tell him.

639
26:58.270 --> 26:59.590
He's an amazing doctor.

640
26:59.590 --> 27:00.790
He can cure anything.

641
27:00.830 --> 27:01.590
Don't exaggerate.

642
27:01.590 --> 27:03.030
I can't even cure myself.

643
27:04.310 --> 27:05.110
What is it?

644
27:11.880 --> 27:13.030
Glioblastoma.

645
27:13.110 --> 27:13.920
What?

646
27:14.110 --> 27:15.000
Say that again!

647
27:22.640 --> 27:23.960
Glioblastoma.

648
27:25.510 --> 27:26.240
See?

649
27:26.790 --> 27:28.830
I told you I'm the chosen one.

650
27:30.270 --> 27:31.200
Awesome, right?

651
27:42.350 --> 27:43.880
W-What kind of tumor?

652
27:43.880 --> 27:45.830
Is it serious?

653
27:46.790 --> 27:49.450
When we get back, let me take a look at your scans.

654
28:03.710 --> 28:08.930
[Dream Garden Themed Hotel]

655
28:14.790 --> 28:16.790
Could it be a misdiagnosis?

656
28:21.110 --> 28:22.510
I've been to 3 hospitals,

657
28:23.590 --> 28:25.790
and they all gave me the same diagnosis.

658
28:27.160 --> 28:28.620
Go to Shanghai right away.

659
28:29.000 --> 28:30.350
I'll give you 2 phone numbers.

660
28:30.350 --> 28:31.790
They're both experts in this field.

661
28:31.790 --> 28:33.850
Make an appointment with one of them.

662
28:34.070 --> 28:34.680
Forget it.

663
28:36.000 --> 28:37.800
I don't want to waste that money.

664
28:38.030 --> 28:38.680
Hey.

665
28:39.590 --> 28:40.580
Do you even realize

666
28:40.580 --> 28:42.310
how serious your condition is?

667
28:42.510 --> 28:43.730
It's been a year

668
28:43.750 --> 28:44.790
since your last checkup.

669
28:44.790 --> 28:45.490
Do you know

670
28:45.520 --> 28:47.850
-that any moment, you could just... -Die.

671
28:48.680 --> 28:49.480
I know.

672
28:51.000 --> 28:52.400
But can chemotherapy

673
28:52.480 --> 28:53.680
cure it at this point?

674
28:56.070 --> 28:57.350
Every doctor

675
28:58.920 --> 29:00.350
has told me clearly

676
29:01.240 --> 29:02.500
that it can't be cured.

677
29:03.310 --> 29:03.920
But...

678
29:05.680 --> 29:07.400
But it could at least

679
29:07.400 --> 29:09.270
extend your life.

680
29:11.350 --> 29:12.160
Extend it?

681
29:19.000 --> 29:20.460
I'm only 18 this year, bro.

682
29:22.070 --> 29:23.530
What good would 1 or 2 years

683
29:23.680 --> 29:24.750
do me?

684
29:28.590 --> 29:29.920
You have to at least try.

685
29:34.550 --> 29:36.510
Bro, Sis.

686
29:38.590 --> 29:39.510
I've tried.

687
29:55.550 --> 29:56.110
I'm...

688
29:58.640 --> 29:59.590
the chosen one.

689
30:01.590 --> 30:02.520
There's no cure.

690
30:06.400 --> 30:07.200
I just

691
30:08.160 --> 30:09.690
want to spend whatever time

692
30:10.030 --> 30:11.270
I have left

693
30:11.960 --> 30:14.160
without making her waste a fortune on me

694
30:16.000 --> 30:17.160
or putting myself through

695
30:17.160 --> 30:18.290
all that suffering.

696
30:20.000 --> 30:22.130
I want to use the little time I have left

697
30:22.680 --> 30:24.750
to enjoy life

698
30:25.790 --> 30:26.550
and do things

699
30:26.550 --> 30:27.880
I've never done before.

700
30:36.350 --> 30:37.810
But you can't just give up.

701
30:39.270 --> 30:41.270
You shamelessly followed me around

702
30:41.350 --> 30:42.160
because you saw

703
30:42.160 --> 30:43.590
on my resume

704
30:43.680 --> 30:46.110
that I'm an expert in the Neurosurgical Department, right?

705
30:46.110 --> 30:47.970
You wanted me to treat you, right?

706
30:48.160 --> 30:49.310
So let me treat you.

707
30:53.160 --> 30:53.830
I did

708
30:53.830 --> 30:55.630
shamelessly follow you around.

709
30:56.310 --> 30:57.240
But like I said,

710
30:58.030 --> 30:58.920
no one can do it.

711
30:59.790 --> 31:00.720
There's no cure.

712
31:02.720 --> 31:03.720
I just...

713
31:05.110 --> 31:06.830
I just wanted to stay

714
31:06.830 --> 31:07.830
close to a doctor.

715
31:09.200 --> 31:11.130
Maybe it'd bring me some good luck.

716
31:11.680 --> 31:12.440
Or maybe one day,

717
31:12.440 --> 31:14.200
if I collapsed in the street,

718
31:15.270 --> 31:16.670
you'd be there to save me,

719
31:17.000 --> 31:17.750
right?

720
31:24.830 --> 31:25.890
Does your mom know?

721
31:34.550 --> 31:36.280
There's no need for her to know.

722
31:38.790 --> 31:39.680
I get it now.

723
31:40.640 --> 31:41.440
I was wondering why you

724
31:41.440 --> 31:43.720
always did such rebellious things before,

725
31:43.720 --> 31:44.400
always doing things

726
31:44.400 --> 31:45.790
your mom hates.

727
31:46.310 --> 31:49.000
Actually, you were deliberately pushing her away.

728
31:49.000 --> 31:50.240
You were worried that if she found out the truth,

729
31:50.240 --> 31:51.200
she wouldn't be able to handle it

730
31:51.200 --> 31:52.660
and would be heartbroken.

731
31:53.160 --> 31:53.960
So you deliberately

732
31:53.960 --> 31:55.360
cut ties with her, right?

733
32:04.790 --> 32:06.250
You even figured that out?

734
32:08.590 --> 32:09.790
You really are no ordinary person.

735
32:09.790 --> 32:10.680
How childish.

736
32:11.960 --> 32:12.830
She's your mom.

737
32:14.270 --> 32:14.960
No matter what you do,

738
32:14.960 --> 32:16.620
she'll still be heartbroken.

739
32:36.510 --> 32:37.720
I'm childish?

740
32:40.680 --> 32:41.310
Bro.

741
32:43.640 --> 32:44.680
Do I have a choice?

742
32:46.920 --> 32:48.270
I'm an adult.

743
32:49.240 --> 32:51.110
I can make

744
32:51.110 --> 32:52.350
my own choices.

745
32:54.550 --> 32:55.480
This is my home,

746
32:56.920 --> 32:58.920
and I've only known you for a couple of days.

747
32:58.920 --> 32:59.750
What gives you the right

748
32:59.750 --> 33:00.880
to tell me what to do?

749
33:02.200 --> 33:04.400
Who are you to make that decision for me?

750
33:06.200 --> 33:06.960
I'm not talking to you.

751
33:06.960 --> 33:08.560
I'm going to talk to your mom.

752
33:11.070 --> 33:12.110
You have no idea

753
33:12.510 --> 33:13.680
how many tricks I pulled

754
33:13.680 --> 33:14.550
and how much effort I put in

755
33:14.550 --> 33:15.440
just to keep it from her.

756
33:15.440 --> 33:16.680
How long can you keep it a secret, huh?

757
33:16.680 --> 33:17.550
How long?

758
33:17.550 --> 33:19.480
Better to suffer a short pain than a long one!

759
33:19.480 --> 33:21.480
But she'll find out sooner or later.

760
33:22.750 --> 33:23.550
Zhou Zheng.

761
33:24.030 --> 33:25.240
If you really treat me as your friend,

762
33:25.240 --> 33:26.100
get out of my way

763
33:26.110 --> 33:27.570
and let me talk to your mom.

764
33:28.310 --> 33:29.160
I don't want my mom

765
33:29.160 --> 33:30.420
spending my final days

766
33:30.750 --> 33:32.750
worrying about me every single day.

767
33:33.070 --> 33:33.920
You know?

768
33:37.750 --> 33:38.440
Bro.

769
33:39.440 --> 33:40.370
I'm telling you,

770
33:43.680 --> 33:45.080
this is the last decision

771
33:45.750 --> 33:47.150
I'll ever make in my life.

772
33:49.240 --> 33:50.350
My last one.

773
33:53.590 --> 33:54.550
Don't push me.

774
33:55.880 --> 33:56.830
Don't push me.

775
34:02.310 --> 34:03.880
Just respect his choice.

776
34:08.280 --> 34:09.810
What are you arguing about?

777
34:12.630 --> 34:13.670
Don't. Don't...

778
34:14.880 --> 34:15.810
I'm begging you.

779
34:17.550 --> 34:18.480
I'm begging you.

780
34:19.360 --> 34:20.400
Please.

781
34:21.230 --> 34:22.280
Please.

782
34:30.510 --> 34:32.239
What's all this arguing about?

783
34:32.320 --> 34:33.550
What are you doing?

784
34:34.550 --> 34:36.710
We didn't get to act our hearts out on set today,

785
34:36.710 --> 34:38.110
so we're rehearsing now.

786
34:39.960 --> 34:40.760
Rehearsing?

787
34:40.880 --> 34:42.360
I-It was pretty intense.

788
34:44.110 --> 34:45.510
What's wrong? What do you need?

789
34:45.510 --> 34:46.440
Are you okay?

790
34:47.110 --> 34:48.630
What do you mean, am I okay?

791
34:50.630 --> 34:51.760
Not everything's about you, okay?

792
34:51.760 --> 34:52.320
You...

793
34:52.870 --> 34:54.590
-Let's rehearse for a little longer. -Come on. Get out.

794
34:54.590 --> 34:55.850
Why are you pushing me?

795
34:56.920 --> 34:58.580
Don't come over for no reason.

796
35:13.590 --> 35:19.910
[Fire Evacuation Plan]

797
35:22.650 --> 35:28.410
[Storefront for Lease]

798
35:49.840 --> 35:50.630
Can't sleep?

799
35:53.070 --> 35:54.400
I see you can't, either.

800
36:00.360 --> 36:01.960
How could this happen to him?

801
36:03.670 --> 36:05.000
He's still so young.

802
36:06.030 --> 36:07.030
You must have seen

803
36:08.320 --> 36:10.120
more cases like this than I have.

804
36:24.360 --> 36:25.760
There's a hospital in Guilin

805
36:25.760 --> 36:27.760
that asked me to go for an interview.

806
36:27.800 --> 36:29.060
I'm leaving tomorrow.

807
36:37.840 --> 36:40.840
You just found out that he's sick, and you're leaving?

808
36:44.760 --> 36:46.760
What's the point of staying anyway?

809
36:47.840 --> 36:48.710
He's right.

810
36:50.030 --> 36:51.560
His illness can't be cured,

811
36:52.480 --> 36:54.410
and that day could come at any time.

812
36:54.840 --> 36:56.640
I don't want to see him like that.

813
36:57.550 --> 36:58.880
While we're not that close,

814
36:58.880 --> 37:00.360
the sooner I leave, the better.

815
37:00.360 --> 37:01.820
You're just running away—

816
37:02.070 --> 37:03.550
running as far away as possible.

817
37:03.550 --> 37:05.750
When faced with a problem I can't solve,

818
37:05.920 --> 37:07.580
what else can I do but run away?

819
37:17.880 --> 37:18.710
Running away

820
37:18.960 --> 37:20.230
will become a habit.

821
37:23.280 --> 37:24.740
And eventually, even when

822
37:25.230 --> 37:26.070
a problem can be solved,

823
37:26.070 --> 37:27.470
you'll still run from it.

824
37:51.840 --> 37:53.370
In my career, the first time

825
37:54.250 --> 37:55.580
I ever had a patient

826
37:55.600 --> 37:56.920
die in front of me

827
37:58.880 --> 38:00.030
was when...

828
38:00.880 --> 38:02.360
When I was an intern.

829
38:02.920 --> 38:04.440
It was an old man.

830
38:06.360 --> 38:07.230
My attending told me

831
38:07.230 --> 38:08.150
he'd come in

832
38:08.150 --> 38:09.630
every winter,

833
38:10.960 --> 38:13.560
and he'd eat 2 servings of rice rolls every day.

834
38:15.480 --> 38:17.410
But during the few days I was there,

835
38:18.710 --> 38:20.710
he could only manage 1 serving a day.

836
38:22.400 --> 38:23.630
My attending said

837
38:26.510 --> 38:28.040
he didn't have long to live,

838
38:28.670 --> 38:29.800
but he did nothing.

839
38:31.480 --> 38:32.410
And sure enough,

840
38:34.230 --> 38:35.280
a few days later,

841
38:35.880 --> 38:37.320
the old man passed away.

842
38:39.880 --> 38:40.670
You see,

843
38:41.070 --> 38:42.670
that's how things often are.

844
38:43.480 --> 38:46.030
Sometimes, you already know how things will end,

845
38:46.030 --> 38:48.830
but there's still nothing you can do to prevent it.

846
38:49.480 --> 38:50.630
This is true of life,

847
38:51.070 --> 38:52.730
and it's true of death as well.

848
38:55.030 --> 38:55.880
You're right.

849
38:58.880 --> 39:00.030
Everyone dies.

850
39:02.890 --> 39:04.410
But that doesn't mean

851
39:04.440 --> 39:06.370
there's nothing we can do about it.

852
39:07.030 --> 39:08.880
Someone has to do something, right?

853
39:08.880 --> 39:10.320
Even if we know we can't change the outcome,

854
39:10.320 --> 39:11.480
we should still try.

855
39:14.670 --> 39:16.870
Otherwise, what's the point of living?

856
39:24.760 --> 39:26.620
Is that what you wanted to tell me?

857
39:30.070 --> 39:30.880
It's not.

858
39:50.710 --> 39:51.640
Liu Zhengliang.

859
39:57.480 --> 39:58.920
This is my first time

860
40:00.670 --> 40:02.870
spending New Year's Eve away from home.

861
40:16.920 --> 40:17.980
The New Year's bell

862
40:18.000 --> 40:19.760
is about to ring.

863
40:19.920 --> 40:22.590
Let's count down together!

864
40:22.840 --> 40:23.710
Ten.

865
40:23.960 --> 40:24.840
Nine.

866
40:25.070 --> 40:25.960
Eight.

867
40:26.070 --> 40:26.960
Seven.

868
40:27.230 --> 40:28.110
Six.

869
40:28.320 --> 40:29.150
Five.

870
40:29.400 --> 40:30.150
Four.

871
40:30.440 --> 40:31.110
Three.

872
40:31.480 --> 40:32.150
Two.

873
40:32.400 --> 40:33.480
One.

874
40:33.800 --> 40:35.550
Happy New Year!

875
40:35.710 --> 40:36.880
Happy New Year!

876
40:39.410 --> 40:46.540
♪ It's only after something is lost that we begin to see ♪

877
40:48.350 --> 40:54.130
♪ But some things can never be undone ♪

878
40:57.330 --> 41:03.720
♪ When snowflakes cover all our yesterdays ♪

879
41:04.970 --> 41:11.000
♪ Perhaps it's best we leave the words unsaid ♪

880
41:14.860 --> 41:22.020
♪ We were once someone else ♪

881
41:23.690 --> 41:29.740
♪ Then, one day, we found our truest selves ♪

882
41:26.280 --> 41:27.070
Check out, please.

883
41:27.070 --> 41:27.710
Okay.

884
41:32.580 --> 41:39.490
♪ Turns out, you don't have to fall apart ♪

885
41:32.630 --> 41:34.110
Has my friend left?

886
41:35.000 --> 41:37.030
She checked out early in the morning.

887
41:37.030 --> 41:38.230
Here's your deposit.

888
41:40.230 --> 41:47.820
♪ To deserve a fresh start ♪

889
41:48.000 --> 41:48.960
Thank you.

890
41:52.110 --> 41:54.640
Thank you for hanging around with Zhou Zheng.

891
41:55.360 --> 41:57.920
My son doesn't have many friends.

892
41:58.800 --> 42:00.760
He was really happy spending these past few days

893
42:00.760 --> 42:01.800
with you.

894
42:02.920 --> 42:03.710
Thank you.

895
42:14.400 --> 42:15.400
This is my number.

896
42:15.920 --> 42:17.190
If you have anything you want to ask,

897
42:17.190 --> 42:18.120
call me anytime.

898
42:26.000 --> 42:32.750
♪ Not every goodbye is meant to erase the past ♪

899
42:34.770 --> 42:41.730
♪ At least we met with open hearts ♪

900
42:36.110 --> 42:39.280
[May Your Journey Be Safe and the New Year Bring Joy to Your Door]

901
42:43.470 --> 42:46.270
♪ When life stretches on for so long ♪

902
42:47.010 --> 42:50.800
♪ Not every story needs a perfect ending ♪

903
42:51.410 --> 42:59.540
♪ Maybe walking side by side for a while is enough ♪

904
43:00.600 --> 43:11.570
♪ I'll keep those words we never got to say in my heart ♪
